From 6875dfc8853546121b48aa33eb17ccc74c222caa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:55:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): name the uncut Z range of a whole-model contour ring
 that has no floor level

A band of a whole-model 2D Contour that stops at the next flat level cuts
the floor passes of the rings that have a floor level. An outer ring of
the same band with no floor level got no pass, and its note was dropped
(forward_band_notes drops outer-ring notes when the contour continues).
The region stayed uncut with no word, in the first band and in an
in-between band.

The band now gives one note for each such ring. The note names the ring
and the Z range that is not cut.

Pinned by first_band_names_the_uncut_range_of_the_ring_without_a_floor_level
and in_between_band_names_the_uncut_range_of_the_ring_without_a_floor_level
(crates/motion/tests/contour_whole_no_floor.rs).

Fixes #2538

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
